Z||000000||BlackARROW||05-08-2001||09:20 PM||||I put only Super in for gas, I saw somewhere on the web, a site about Fiero's, that it would be best to adjust the timing of some degrees to get the most out of the super.  Last week I tried mid gas (89 octane), and I think it was less pinking. Maybe it's because of that unapropriate timing for the 91 points of octane in the super I usually use.  <BR>First, do you prefer putting Super? Some people tell me it makes no difference, but I think my Super (even for an old '85) is more effecient. <P>I've search through the old topics, but didn't find any info about something concerning the timing change.  <P>Stay Sharp!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>BA-&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85||||reg||1
Z||000001||maninblack||05-08-2001||10:32 PM||||well, I use 94 octane on my 87, maybe its in my heart but i do feel the differance during<BR>WOT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||05-08-2001||10:37 PM||||I use 93 oct. in mine every tank. I definatly see a huge decrease in gas milage when I use regular 89-lower. I get like 17+ mpg city with 93, and 13+ mpg city with regular. I would also say I feel a small difference in power output. I do notice smoother idle definatly.||||reg||1
Z||000003||BlackARROW||05-09-2001||12:41 AM||||I just calculate some mpg's.  I tried a home-made ram-air as a test, which lowered my MPG to 25 (octane 94).  Next tank was Oct.89, and I made 28 MPG.  Now I'm running on 91 again, then I'll try with my fiberglass home-made ram-air (I shall do it tomorrow), and then I'll try 91 + one little bottle which highers the rate to 96-98  (hmm.. maybe should I try with an original 94 + 5/7 ?  That would be an interesting test for gas Octane signification.<P>Have fun filling your tank, now that the gas price is so high  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   In a way, I'm happy to be running only a 4-cylinders :P  hehe<P>Stay cool!<P>------------------<BR>BA-&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85||||reg||1
